        "scene": "myth",
        "text": "The shopkeeper says paying by UPI above ₹2,000 now costs me extra!",
        "start": 0.27,
        "seconds": 4.51,
        "window": 4.83,
        "fill": 0.934
      },
      {
        "scene": "actually",
        "text": "Actually, that fee is called MDR. It is charged to the shop, not to you.",
        "start": 5.1,
        "seconds": 4.42,
        "window": 4.8,
        "fill": 0.921
      },
      {
        "scene": "plan",
        "text": "The plan is a fee of 0.4% on shop payments above ₹2,000.",
        "start": 9.9,
        "seconds": 5.01,
        "window": 5.47,
        "fill": 0.916
      },
      {
        "scene": "bill",
        "text": "So on a bill of ₹5,000, the shop's bank keeps ₹20. Your bill stays ₹5,000.",
        "start": 15.37,
        "seconds": 6.08,
        "window": 6.67,
        "fill": 0.912
      },
      {
        "scene": "free",
        "text": "Sending money to a friend stays free. And the shop fee is a cost for the shop, not a charge on you.",
        "start": 22.03,
        "seconds": 5.5,
        "window": 5.9,
        "fill": 0.932
      },
      {
        "scene": "status",
        "text": "And right now, it isn't even live. It has been put off until after Diwali.",
